      "id": 489706,
      "username": "Ayesha",
      "name": "",
      "created_at": "2025-12-29T07:56:26.018Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hello All,</p>\n<p>I have a question regarding Tax Calculations.<br>\nI have an item with two Item Tax Templates defined: one for sales transactions and one for purchase transactions. However, when performing a transaction, ERPNext always fetches only the first Item Tax Template defined on the item.</p>\n<p>I attempted to address this by adding two checkboxes on the Item Tax Template, Input and Output, and implementing a client script to select the Input template for purchase transactions and the Output template for sales transactions. However, this logic is being overridden by ERPNext’s standard functionality.</p>\n<p>What is the recommended approach to handle this scenario?<br>\nPlease note that within the same transaction, there can be both taxable and non-taxable items.</p>",
